      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T09:51:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC this is so that you can set `updatable: true` on vendor apexes, which I think is not what we should ideally aim for? I think it\u0027d be better to have a separate attribute that enforces the invariants you want for vendor apexes (called something better than \"updatable\"!)",
      "revId": "9cd979a7fb86c21f22d52eebf5c47ea2c8ec5ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a050072_b413e709",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T00:46:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we just use `updatable`? I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a good idea to introduce yet another property for \"updatability\", which is already served by `updatable` property. Instead, I think, if necessary, we\u0027d better have a new property for, for example, \"membership\"?\n\nWhat do you think, Jingwen?",
      "parentUuid": "207b2746_c628a00b",
      "revId": "9cd979a7fb86c21f22d52eebf5c47ea2c8ec5ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21b6c3a9_7dbf7deb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1514900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T08:04:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it would be confusing if `updatable` meant something different with vendor apexes. I\u0027ve always associated `updatable` with Mainline modules, which has a clear set of checks and requirements. Similar to what Anton said in https://b.corp.google.com/issues/274041915#comment11.\n\nIs there a document somewhere that describes the key differences of updatable Mainline APEXes and updatable Vendor APEXes? It would help if these differences were clearly spelled out so we can reflect them at the build system level too, instead of implicitly toggling checks.",
      "parentUuid": "5a050072_b413e709",
      "revId": "9cd979a7fb86c21f22d52eebf5c47ea2c8ec5ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "880182f1_59aa65ac",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T08:30:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`checkUpdatable` is the key place where the \"updatability\" requirements are defined:\n(https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/refs/heads/master:build/soong/apex/apex.go;drc\u003d7346c436e5a11ce08f6a80dcfeb8ef941ca30176;l\u003d3022?q\u003dcheckUpdatable)\n\n- should set `min_sdk_version`: cc modules rely on this to enable compile-time check on accidental access to new symbols.\n- should NOT set `use_platform_apis`: platform apis are not public API surface.\n- should NOT set `use_vndk_as_stable`: VNDK can\u0027t be used across releases.\n- should NOT set `future_updatable`\n- `classpath_fragments` should set `generate_classpaths_proto`\n- Java deps should use \"stable\" sdk version\n\nFor these checks vendor apexes are not that different from other updatable apexes. Those requirements shouldn\u0027t be specific to \"mainline\" apexes. \n\nHowever, allowed_deps check is not related to whether an apex is updatable or not. It\u0027s more like \"FYI\".\n\nI\u0027m not adding a special meaning to `updatable`. Instead, if we need a property to indicate a mainline module, then I think we need to be more explicit about it instead of relying \"updatable apex\".",
      "parentUuid": "21b6c3a9_7dbf7deb",
      "revId": "9cd979a7fb86c21f22d52eebf5c47ea2c8ec5ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9856786e_696338bb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-26T08:51:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll abandon this change.\n\nBut I\u0027d like to claim that `updatable` shouldn\u0027t be used as a synonym for \"mainline\".\n\nMy suggestion is either\n- to use `is_mainline` (which can enforce `updatable`, by definition)\n- or, to use \"system \u0026\u0026 `updatable`\" (see below)\n\n\n```\n                     APEX\n     \n          |  updatable  | not updatable\n----------|-------------|---------------\nsystem    |             |\n----------|-------------|---------------\nother     |             |\npartition |             |\n----------|-------------|---------------\n```",
      "parentUuid": "880182f1_59aa65ac",
      "revId": "9cd979a7fb86c21f22d52eebf5c47ea2c8ec5ddc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
